1
00:00:43,544 --> 00:00:44,753
Mr. President.

2
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:51,218
Uh, sir?

3
00:01:42,728 --> 00:01:43,895
Kitae.

4
00:01:51,403 --> 00:01:52,738
Don't touch me!

5
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,119
What's going on?

6
00:02:02,706 --> 00:02:03,790
Is he dead?

7
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:07,961
Yes.

8
00:02:10,297 --> 00:02:11,673
It was Cho, wasn't it?

9
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:14,551
Yeah.

10
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:18,721
Cho, that lunatic!

11
00:02:18,722 --> 00:02:21,725
I knew he was going to do something.

12
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:25,729
But to murder the President…

13
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:27,814
him and Chief Gwak…

14
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:45,957
What happened to Director Cho?

15
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:53,650
OCTOBER 27,
MILITARY SECURITY COMMAND

16
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,374
PRESIDENTIAL ASSASSINATION…

17
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:21,928
Deputy Director, good afternoon.

18
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:27,142
I've been assigned to this investigation.
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Baek.

19
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:33,732
You were at the Gungjeong-dong safe house
after the incident, is that correct?

20
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:44,034
So why did you show up there?

21
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:55,669
Your name wasn't
on the guest list for the dinner.

22
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:58,799
What time did you arrive last night?

23
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:02,469
Colonel Ahn Jaeho.

24
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:05,722
We're beginning the process.

25
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:08,307
Who did you come with?

26
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:10,143
Yes, sir. But, is there…

27
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,979
a specific reason Colonel Baek was, um,

28
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,315
assigned to this post?

29
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:18,860
Deputy Director,

30
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:21,613
were you involved
in the President's murder?

31
00:05:29,204 --> 00:05:31,414
If you would prefer to sit here
and remain silent,

32
00:05:32,249 --> 00:05:34,709
we'll assume that you're admitting
to criminal charges.

33
00:05:35,544 --> 00:05:36,586
Is that what you want?

34
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,924
What are you doing? Who made you do this?

35
00:05:49,224 --> 00:05:50,225
Deputy Director…

36
00:05:51,101 --> 00:05:53,227
Look, I think maybe
you're not grasping this…

37
00:05:53,228 --> 00:05:56,857
Your superior shot and killed
the President and you were there!

38
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:06,825
Ugh, I'm full.

39
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:27,387
Hey, you in there!

40
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,222
Can you hear me?

41
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:31,515
Listen carefully.

42
00:06:31,516 --> 00:06:34,144
Call up General Jang Mujin.
Do it immediately.

43
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,521
And ask him who captured Director Cho.

44
00:06:37,564 --> 00:06:38,857
All right?

45
00:06:57,876 --> 00:07:01,503
Baek Kitae is being questioned
by the Joint Investigation Headquarters?

46
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:04,715
Yes, sir. We heard he was
in Gungjeong-dong that evening.

47
00:07:04,716 --> 00:07:05,883
Yeah, that's right.

48
00:07:05,884 --> 00:07:06,967
…JANG MUJIN

49
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:08,719
Actually saw him myself at the safe house.

50
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:09,970
That's why I called you.

51
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:12,432
We'd just like a chance to
ask some questions, sir.

52
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,352
It won't take long, sir, I promise.

53
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:18,020
What do you need to question him for?

54
00:07:18,021 --> 00:07:20,106
Colonel Ahn, listen here.

55
00:07:21,358 --> 00:07:22,691
I'm listening, sir.

56
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:24,568
Release the Deputy Director.

57
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:26,363
- We can't just let him go without--
- Stop it!

58
00:07:26,905 --> 00:07:28,615
He's the one who captured Director Cho!

59
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,449
What?

60
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,533
If it weren't for him,

61
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:33,828
this country would be
in Cho's hands right now.

62
00:07:38,792 --> 00:07:40,001
You're telling me…

63
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:44,381
you really think I was involved
in assassinating the President?

64
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:49,219
I look like Director Cho to you?
That power-tripping piece of shit.

65
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:55,016
Get your head straight, Baek Kihyun.

66
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,311
Think carefully about who's on your side.

67
00:07:58,812 --> 00:07:59,938
Who's your friend,

68
00:08:01,272 --> 00:08:02,941
and who's your adversary…

69
00:08:19,249 --> 00:08:20,667
Deputy Director, sir…

70
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:22,919
you can leave now.

71
00:08:42,981 --> 00:08:44,440
Let him through.

72
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:45,525
Sir, what happened?

73
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:48,278
He was the person
who captured Director Cho.

74
00:08:58,121 --> 00:09:02,042
KOREAN CENTRAL
INTELLIGENCE AGENCY

75
00:09:23,772 --> 00:09:27,984
Sometimes, one split-second
decision changes the course of history.

76
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:29,861
Sir, wait!

77
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:31,612
Sir!

78
00:09:31,613 --> 00:09:32,947
Wait, sir!

79
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:36,241
- What?
-  Sir.

80
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:38,118
Tell me where you're heading.

81
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:40,621
Well, I'm going to the KCIA.

82
00:09:40,622 --> 00:09:42,539
And what are you planning to do?

83
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:44,834
Uh… I… I don't know.

84
00:09:45,627 --> 00:09:47,002
Wait a minute.

85
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:50,214
Hang on.
So all of the gunshots I heard earlier…

86
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:53,009
Wait… The President is safe, isn't he?

87
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:56,428
Before assassinating
the President,

88
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:59,348
Director Cho had summoned
Army Chief of Staff, Jang Mujin,

89
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:01,433
to the government safe house.

90
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:04,938
His plan was to take Mujin to KCIA
headquarters after the job was finished,

91
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:07,898
and convince him to join his side.

92
00:10:07,899 --> 00:10:09,067
Mr. Cho, please…

93
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:11,277
Report to Army headquarters.

94
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,153
Army headquarters?

95
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:15,073
You'll need the support
of the entire military.

96
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:19,952
Go to Army headquarters.
Both of you wait there.

97
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:21,788
I'll take care of everything at the KCIA.

98
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:24,832
Good plan, we'll drive over now.

99
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:26,458
You handle the KCIA.

100
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,377
Don't worry about a thing.

101
00:10:28,378 --> 00:10:29,921
Make sure you get there quickly.

102
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:33,007
I'll call you ASAP, sir.

103
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:35,510
Let's go! To the Army headquarters!

104
00:10:37,095 --> 00:10:40,056
However, after the deed was done,
Cho started panicking.

105
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:43,142
In the end, he decided to trust me…

106
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:46,396
…and headed straight to the
Army headquarters instead of the KCIA.

107
00:10:47,522 --> 00:10:49,274
This is KCIA Deputy Director Baek Kitae.

108
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,483
Director Cho killed the President.

109
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:53,278
He's on his way to Army headquarters now.

110
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:56,698
As soon as he gets there,
you need to arrest him.

111
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:00,326
Cho murdered the president,
are you listening?

112
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:02,620
Arrest him now!

113
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:07,000
Incompetent son of a bitch.

114
00:11:18,553 --> 00:11:20,513
DEPUTY DIRECTOR BAEK KITAE

115
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:25,058
You've done an excellent job,
Deputy Director Baek.

116
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:27,102
- Well done.
- I was just doing my duty.

117
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:29,730
The KCIA was implicated in this,

118
00:11:29,731 --> 00:11:32,441
so they'll bring in
Joint Investigations for the inquiry.

119
00:11:32,442 --> 00:11:33,693
That concerns me.

120
00:11:34,569 --> 00:11:38,156
A boat that's being rocked
is bound to wind up on the ocean floor.

121
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:39,908
Yes, of course.

122
00:11:41,117 --> 00:11:43,620
Your concerns make sense,
especially in this climate.

123
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:45,330
Mr. Baek.

124
00:11:46,122 --> 00:11:47,831
Effective immediately,

125
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:52,962
I am appointing you acting director
of the Korean Central Intelligence Agency.

126
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:56,673
I'm very flattered, sir.

127
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:58,801
Deputy Director… Oh, sorry.

128
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:01,346
Director Baek, please don't let me down.

129
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:04,974
Hwang Daesik will take over
unless we act fast.

130
00:12:05,475 --> 00:12:08,394
- That man can't be allowed near power.
- Understood, sir.

131
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:35,087
PERSONAL DETAILS
BAEK KITAE

132
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:37,881
Baek Kitae's the one
who captured Director Cho?

133
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:39,132
Yes, sir.

134
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:42,470
Cho was headed to the KCIA,
then Baek lured him away.

135
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:45,974
Ah… That prick.

136
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:47,934
He's pretty clever.

137
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:53,231
Guess there's a reason
he was such an asset to the President.

138
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:55,358
He's acting director now.

139
00:12:56,526 --> 00:12:59,361
He was appointed by
General Jang Mujin this morning.

140
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:04,158
Okay, so General Jang's
trying to keep us in check.

141
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:08,870
Any other intel
from the guy who brought this?

142
00:13:08,871 --> 00:13:10,415
- Yes, sir.
- What did he say?

143
00:13:13,668 --> 00:13:16,003
He's going after Chief Cheon's funding.

144
00:13:16,004 --> 00:13:18,171
All the money
he's getting from the government.

145
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:25,721
That son of a bitch
is pretty clever too, huh?

146
00:13:27,015 --> 00:13:28,599
He's getting out soon.

147
00:13:29,434 --> 00:13:31,019
At least that's what I've heard.

148
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:33,062
Yes, speaking of which,

149
00:13:34,314 --> 00:13:36,441
it's about time
he got into the game again.

150
00:13:37,108 --> 00:13:39,067
For real this time. Don't you think?

151
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,069
Agreed.

152
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:43,363
For real this time. That's right.

153
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:46,158
Get him a position
in the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

154
00:13:46,159 --> 00:13:47,160
Yes, will do, sir.

155
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,204
Jaeho, listen.

156
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:52,206
Sir?

157
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:54,167
You need to realize…

158
00:13:56,544 --> 00:13:58,921
that this assassination is…

159
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:03,217
nothing less than
an opportunity from heaven.

160
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,886
At this time,

161
00:14:05,887 --> 00:14:09,222
head of Martial Law Joint
Investigation Headquarters, Hwang Daesik

162
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:12,727
will deliver an interim briefing
on the assassination of the President.

163
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:21,068
The assassination of the President,

164
00:14:21,069 --> 00:14:23,529
which took place at 7:50 p.m.,

165
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:28,116
on October 26th in a safe house
in the Gungjeong-dong area,

166
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:30,786
was tragically committed in a banquet hall

167
00:14:30,787 --> 00:14:34,248
where KCIA officials met
to discuss matters of national security.

168
00:14:34,916 --> 00:14:38,001
This murder was determined
to be premeditated

169
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:42,006
and carried out by
Mr. Cho Namsik of the KCIA.

170
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:45,967
The motive was Cho's fear of dismissal.

171
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:48,220
He had recently lost the president's trust

172
00:14:48,221 --> 00:14:51,765
and was under scrutiny
by the Presidential Security Service.

173
00:14:51,766 --> 00:14:53,809
His ambition was to seize authority,

174
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,811
and become president himself.

175
00:14:55,812 --> 00:15:00,233
His lust for power and control
drove him to commit this monstrous act.

176
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:01,901
Right now!

177
00:15:03,486 --> 00:15:04,487
Right here!

178
00:15:06,531 --> 00:15:10,868
The KCIA is standing at
the greatest crossroads since inception.

179
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:16,206
This agency was built with the blood
and sweat of our people

180
00:15:16,207 --> 00:15:18,042
and now we're losing their trust!

181
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:20,628
Our very name…

182
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:23,464
Mocked and ridiculed at every turn.

183
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:26,008
From this day on,

184
00:15:27,135 --> 00:15:29,303
our agency will thrive under my command.

185
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:32,431
We'll restore our power,

186
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:36,018
and we will protect
the reputation of the state!

187
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:38,980
If we want to survive, this is how.

188
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:43,818
And that will secure
the future of our great nation.

189
00:15:44,694 --> 00:15:49,406
We consider this the greatest tragedy
and most grievous offense

190
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,742
ever committed under the Yushin regime.

191
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:56,246
In order for us to reestablish
our national security,

192
00:15:56,247 --> 00:16:00,251
all available resources
will be mobilized to prevent recurrence.

193
00:16:01,252 --> 00:16:02,961
We will…

194
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,255
- We will…
- We will…

195
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:06,631
…work in the shadows!

196
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:08,509
- …work in the shadows!
- …work in the shadows!

197
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:10,844
…to defend our sunlit land!

198
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:13,222
- …to defend our sunlit land!
- …to defend our sunlit land!

199
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,974
- Commander!
- General Hwang, sir!

200
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:19,729
Do you have anything to say?
Please, just a brief comment, general!

201
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:23,356
Hwang Daesik, head of
the Joint Investigation Headquarters,

202
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:26,526
will use his investigative powers
to tear the KCIA apart

203
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:28,029
and rise to the center of power.

204
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:31,698
As acting director of the KCIA,

205
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:34,034
I must find a way
to contain the situation,

206
00:16:34,035 --> 00:16:36,036
stop Hwang from taking over,

207
00:16:36,037 --> 00:16:38,288
and reclaim the KCIA's authority.

208
00:16:38,289 --> 00:16:39,581
That's right.

209
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:43,127
The KCIA and the JIH
are in a full-blown dogfight.

210
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:46,338
To our country and its people!

211
00:16:46,339 --> 00:16:47,757
- Here, here!
- Here, here!

212
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:55,263
Hwang Daesik!

213
00:16:55,264 --> 00:17:12,907
- Hwang Daesik!
- Hwang Daesik!

214
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:20,456
The President's dead
and it's time to move forward.

215
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,084
What matters now is…

216
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:25,919
who comes next.

217
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,798
Who's gonna take his seat
and lead this country?

218
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,553
Who do you think will do it?

219
00:17:35,304 --> 00:17:36,472
Someone once said,

220
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:41,477
"Kings are only chosen by the heavens."

221
00:17:42,812 --> 00:17:46,107
And I think
you might be heaven's selection.

222
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:49,026
Come on, what is that?

223
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,958
Hwang's not about to sit and do nothing.

224
00:18:05,293 --> 00:18:07,419
At this point, he's our biggest problem.

225
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:11,590
That bald, oily son of a bitch.
He just wants status and control.

226
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,842
All of the power and authority

227
00:18:13,843 --> 00:18:16,554
can be found in
the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

228
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:21,309
Hwang will use the investigation
to eliminate his political enemies.

229
00:18:22,143 --> 00:18:23,477
Ah, shit.

230
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:28,357
So they'll likely take aim
right at the KCIA from the start.

231
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,234
Exactly.

232
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:38,701
Which means you and I are both gonna be
on his list of targets to get rid of.

233
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:43,997
So what's the plan, Baek?

234
00:18:43,998 --> 00:18:46,959
You gonna let it happen?
You gonna just sit there and take it?

235
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:57,637
Well, sir.

236
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,309
Why don't we…

237
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:06,979
cross the Rubicon together? Join forces.

238
00:19:15,196 --> 00:19:16,781
You mean you want us to…

239
00:19:18,199 --> 00:19:19,825
overthrow the government?

240
00:19:22,787 --> 00:19:25,539
You know how this country is structured.
You've seen it,

241
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,292
from the inside, with the President.

242
00:20:12,503 --> 00:20:13,754
Let's do it.

243
00:20:14,505 --> 00:20:17,006
Yeah. Let's be bold!

244
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:23,472
First off,

245
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:26,433
we need to win over
General Jang's support.

246
00:20:26,434 --> 00:20:29,478
Ugh, well he's not exactly
a pushover, is he?

247
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:31,980
We need the Martial Law Commander
on our side

248
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:33,481
if we're going to take over the military.

249
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:34,525
I know.

250
00:20:35,985 --> 00:20:37,528
And we'll get there.

251
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,951
But first, talk to Choi.

252
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:46,704
Have her bring the money
I entrusted to her.

253
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:49,540
You ever seen anyone turn down money?

254
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:51,667
Those Army bastards…

255
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:54,879
They lose their minds
at the smell of clean cash.

256
00:20:55,463 --> 00:20:57,298
All we have to do is buy them off.

257
00:20:58,591 --> 00:20:59,592
Right. Copy that.

258
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:08,768
Kitae, look.

259
00:21:11,437 --> 00:21:13,772
I 'm counting on you now, all right?

260
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:14,899
And you know…

261
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:25,159
after I move up, you're next.

262
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:35,585
BUSAN DISTRICT
PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

263
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:46,471
Director Cho announced that…

264
00:21:46,472 --> 00:21:48,848
- …would mobilize every resource…
- What does this mean?

265
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:51,893
…at its disposal
to reestablish national discipline

266
00:21:51,894 --> 00:21:56,898
and prevent any further political violence
or unrest in the coming weeks.

267
00:21:56,899 --> 00:21:59,067
Major General Hwang's promise
to the Korean people

268
00:21:59,068 --> 00:22:01,236
- comes amidst widespread complaints…
- Good morning, ma'am.

269
00:22:01,237 --> 00:22:02,655
…of abuse by the--

270
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,115
Taking a break?

271
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,450
Come on, let's go.

272
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:09,494
Get back to work. Now!

273
00:22:09,495 --> 00:22:11,454
- Yes, ma'am.
- Let's get back to it.

274
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:19,421
- Kang, over here.
- Yeah, coming.

275
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:26,386
So Park Changbae,
have you located him yet?

276
00:22:26,387 --> 00:22:30,181
Oh, uh, we're using Kim's statement to
get a general area, then narrow it down,

277
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:32,601
but he's in Seoul, not Busan,
so it's a bit harder.

278
00:22:33,435 --> 00:22:36,396
Uh, and Ms. Oh,
the chief told us to bury this case.

279
00:22:36,397 --> 00:22:38,940
If he finds out about this,
he's going to blow his top.

280
00:22:38,941 --> 00:22:40,650
You sure this is okay?

281
00:22:40,651 --> 00:22:43,903
-  Narcotics Unit, Busan…
-  All right, Changbae,

282
00:22:43,904 --> 00:22:45,573
- where are you?
-  She's here. Understood.

283
00:22:46,532 --> 00:22:47,658
Sorry, excuse me, uh…

284
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:50,619
The chief wants to see you upstairs.

285
00:22:51,954 --> 00:22:53,037
Yes.

286
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:57,042
"Integrity, honesty, humility."

287
00:22:57,793 --> 00:23:02,505
Wow, Chief. That's a really nice
sentiment for what it's worth.

288
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:08,803
You know, Ms. Oh…

289
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:11,306
…it occurred to me that
even though you've been here a while,

290
00:23:11,307 --> 00:23:15,059
I've never treated you to a cup of tea
in my office, not to mention…

291
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:18,062
you're the first female prosecutor
in Korean history.

292
00:23:18,063 --> 00:23:19,773
I should be offering more.

293
00:23:20,566 --> 00:23:23,359
Man or woman, male or female,
we're all prosecutors…

294
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,904
We all have the same title.

295
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:27,323
Hmm…

296
00:23:31,285 --> 00:23:33,954
So, um,
why am I in the principal's office?

297
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:35,705
Mmm…

298
00:23:35,706 --> 00:23:37,540
The Joint Investigation Headquarters

299
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:41,127
is asking us to stop the criminals
who are causing social unrest.

300
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:42,295
You hear about this?

301
00:23:42,296 --> 00:23:44,088
Yes, sounds familiar.

302
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,341
Although, I don't…

303
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:50,386
I don't know why it'd be their purview
to look into something like that, do you?

304
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:52,347
Well, they'd probably say something like,

305
00:23:52,348 --> 00:23:54,724
"We are in an unprecedented
time of crisis,

306
00:23:54,725 --> 00:23:56,601
so if we want to prevent further unrest,

307
00:23:56,602 --> 00:23:59,854
prosecutors should expand
the scope of their job

308
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:01,106
as a duty to the country."

309
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:05,653
Anyway, on that note,
remember that narcotics case you had?

310
00:24:06,779 --> 00:24:08,906
The one that's been shut down for a while…

311
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:11,575
You wanna maybe reopen it?

312
00:24:18,082 --> 00:24:19,291
All of a sudden?

313
00:24:20,334 --> 00:24:22,752
Why? Why reopen it?

314
00:24:22,753 --> 00:24:24,837
Well, it was your case originally, right?

315
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:27,132
Yeah, sure. It was, but still, sir…

316
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:34,889
Was this an order you got
from a director way up the flagpole?

317
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,641
What are you talking about, Ms. Oh?

318
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:39,311
We're supposed to be
prosecuting drug crimes, regardless.

319
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:43,690
And if we're gonna do it,
might as well go for broke.

320
00:24:43,691 --> 00:24:47,111
We'll support with every resource
our office can give.

321
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:49,196
Do you mean that, sir?

322
00:24:50,698 --> 00:24:52,031
Please don't be generous

323
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:54,367
if you're gonna go back on your word
and break your promise.

324
00:24:54,368 --> 00:24:56,411
Hey. Have I ever done that, Ms. Oh?

325
00:24:56,412 --> 00:24:57,912
Yes, many times.

326
00:24:59,415 --> 00:25:01,582
I'm serious in this case.

327
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:04,127
The people at Joint Investigations
need a prosecutor,

328
00:25:04,128 --> 00:25:05,962
and they specifically requested you.

329
00:25:05,963 --> 00:25:07,338
Is that a joke?

330
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:08,423
No.

331
00:25:08,424 --> 00:25:09,882
Why me though?

332
00:25:09,883 --> 00:25:11,343
How should I know?

333
00:25:12,553 --> 00:25:14,512
But… Mmm…

334
00:25:14,513 --> 00:25:18,308
You happen to know someone there?
Over at the JIH?

335
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:21,020
Not at all.

336
00:25:37,995 --> 00:25:40,497
Whoa.

337
00:26:02,728 --> 00:26:05,271
JOINT INVESTIGATION HEADQUARTERS
INVESTIGATION DIVISION

338
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:13,988
Investigate thoroughly
and tell your men to keep security tight.

339
00:26:13,989 --> 00:26:15,824
- Understood?
-  Yes, sir.

340
00:26:20,496 --> 00:26:21,872
Prosecutor Oh Yejin?

341
00:26:24,208 --> 00:26:26,251
I'm Colonel Ahn,
Chief of Security Department.

342
00:26:27,544 --> 00:26:28,545
Oh Yejin, nice to meet you.

343
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:31,048
This way.

344
00:26:53,153 --> 00:26:54,655
You can wait here, Ms. Oh.

345
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:57,991
Ah, also…

346
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:01,828
I've heard positive things
from the advisor.

347
00:27:01,829 --> 00:27:02,996
I'm excited to work with you.

348
00:27:03,789 --> 00:27:05,039
The advisor?

349
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:06,416
He'll be here in a moment.

350
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:10,921
The advisor?

351
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:16,634
Geez, could they make it
any darker in here?

352
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:18,095
Looks like a damn crypt.

353
00:27:40,868 --> 00:27:42,870
SPECIAL ADVISOR JANG GEONYOUNG

354
00:27:55,257 --> 00:27:58,342
Congratulations
on the promotion, Director.

355
00:27:58,343 --> 00:27:59,887
So, what are you doing in Seoul?

356
00:28:00,929 --> 00:28:03,599
Well, they transferred me
as deputy director.

357
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:08,312
They promoted you,
so your old job opened up.

358
00:28:11,273 --> 00:28:12,982
I'm your replacement.

359
00:28:12,983 --> 00:28:16,612
You're number one, and I'm number two.

360
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:19,364
Hang on.

361
00:28:21,450 --> 00:28:23,285
Chief Cheon didn't tell you, did he?

362
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:27,039
Sorry.
I just assumed you already knew.

363
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:31,251
He really didn't discuss it with you
at all?

364
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:34,546
Wow. Man.

365
00:28:35,172 --> 00:28:37,382
That's not right.
He screwed up on that one.

366
00:28:41,428 --> 00:28:42,638
It's a big office.

367
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:49,478
Well, I'm sure he had his reasons
for bringing you in.

368
00:28:51,355 --> 00:28:54,149
So do your job well.
And stay out of trouble.

369
00:28:54,900 --> 00:28:56,360
Yes, sir. Director.

370
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:59,655
Oh, by the way,
I heard you got interrogated.

371
00:29:02,866 --> 00:29:05,284
Hauled you
into Joint Investigation Headquarters.

372
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:07,287
Sounds like
General Hwang's out to get you.

373
00:29:07,788 --> 00:29:09,664
Know what people have
been calling him lately?

374
00:29:09,665 --> 00:29:11,290
The Bald Rhino.

375
00:29:11,291 --> 00:29:12,875
Correct!

376
00:29:12,876 --> 00:29:17,004
He's so determined that he'll bulldoze
over everything in his way

377
00:29:17,005 --> 00:29:18,381
to get what he wants.

378
00:29:18,382 --> 00:29:22,427
He throws all his weight at the problem
and rams ahead until he reaches his goal.

379
00:29:23,011 --> 00:29:24,804
He's bald, too, so yeah.

380
00:29:24,805 --> 00:29:27,139
Lot of bald guys are like that.

381
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:28,767
But honestly, here's the problem.

382
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:33,021
The agency's rep has
been pretty bad lately.

383
00:29:33,647 --> 00:29:35,482
You really think we can win against Hwang?

384
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:38,819
What do you think, sir?

385
00:29:55,585 --> 00:29:56,586
Hmm?

386
00:30:16,565 --> 00:30:18,400
Want me to send you back to Busan?

387
00:30:18,984 --> 00:30:21,778
'Cause it's starting to feel like
you're here to antagonize me.

388
00:30:22,654 --> 00:30:23,655
Well?

389
00:30:24,990 --> 00:30:26,074
Hey.

390
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:28,201
Pyo Haksu.

391
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:31,204
You bald little rat.

392
00:30:36,001 --> 00:30:37,460
Yes, Kitae?

393
00:30:37,461 --> 00:30:39,004
"Yes, sir."

394
00:30:40,088 --> 00:30:41,423
Sir, I'm sorry.

395
00:30:42,799 --> 00:30:44,384
You better get it together.

396
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:48,055
Understood, I'm very sorry.

397
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:51,433
CHIEF OF SECURITY DEPARTMENT
AHN JAEHO

398
00:30:52,976 --> 00:30:55,102
- Ah, you're here.
- Oh. Let me get that, sir.

399
00:30:55,103 --> 00:30:56,229
Oh, yeah, thanks.

400
00:30:58,690 --> 00:30:59,983
What's this box for?

401
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:01,693
Oh, that?

402
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:03,987
Ah, well,

403
00:31:04,571 --> 00:31:07,491
Chief Cheon's slush fund,
we're keeping a paper trail on it.

404
00:31:09,493 --> 00:31:10,744
You want the assignment?

405
00:31:12,579 --> 00:31:14,247
Is there some reason you're choosing me?

406
00:31:15,290 --> 00:31:17,626
Well, you're…
you're the smartest one here.

407
00:31:19,044 --> 00:31:20,045
It's true.

408
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:25,926
Special orders from the commander,
so be diligent, all right?

409
00:31:26,510 --> 00:31:29,386
Go through these, figure out
the full extent of the slush fund

410
00:31:29,387 --> 00:31:30,597
and report back.

411
00:31:32,891 --> 00:31:34,142
Yes, sir. Of course.

412
00:32:07,968 --> 00:32:09,051
MILITARY SECURITY COMMAND

413
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:10,679
PERSONAL RECORD - 1. PERSONAL
DETAILS - NAME: BAEK KITAE

414
00:32:15,559 --> 00:32:19,771
9 YEARS EARLIER, BUSAN

415
00:32:20,397 --> 00:32:22,440
I heard you joined Security Command.

416
00:32:24,025 --> 00:32:26,069
Tell me why you asked to see me, sir.

417
00:32:29,573 --> 00:32:31,992
What did Jang Geonyoung say
when he visited you?

418
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:37,664
Did you see me in Saigon? See what I did?

419
00:32:39,666 --> 00:32:40,667
Yes, I remember.

420
00:32:41,251 --> 00:32:44,296
So what are you going to do now?
Try to take me down?

421
00:32:47,465 --> 00:32:48,592
Look, Kihyun.

422
00:32:49,217 --> 00:32:50,594
You need to choose.

423
00:32:54,639 --> 00:32:56,349
If I did come after you,

424
00:32:58,310 --> 00:32:59,895
what would you do about it?

425
00:33:03,773 --> 00:33:05,650
Well, if it weren't for me,

426
00:33:07,194 --> 00:33:09,070
you think you'd be where you are now?

427
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,241
What?

428
00:33:13,742 --> 00:33:15,243
Am I wrong here?

429
00:33:17,787 --> 00:33:19,206
You threatening me?

430
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:26,171
I won't consider you family
if you decide to get aggressive with this.

431
00:33:27,047 --> 00:33:29,174
Either you go down, or I do.

432
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:31,801
Or maybe we both will.

433
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:35,764
So I would think of your family

434
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:39,601
when you're choosing
which route to take here.

435
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:43,980
Just like I did

436
00:33:46,191 --> 00:33:47,400
for Soyeong

437
00:33:48,902 --> 00:33:49,986
and for you.

438
00:34:28,358 --> 00:34:29,859
Who was it anyway?

439
00:34:30,568 --> 00:34:32,988
Who exactly ordered my interrogation?

440
00:34:33,738 --> 00:34:35,740
Colonel Ahn gave the assignment.

441
00:34:38,827 --> 00:34:40,412
So he put you to the test

442
00:34:41,371 --> 00:34:43,123
to see how you'd react.

443
00:34:48,878 --> 00:34:50,463
Any other information?

444
00:34:52,674 --> 00:34:54,259
He hasn't said very much.

445
00:34:57,053 --> 00:35:00,765
They'll keep pressuring you,
the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

446
00:35:02,726 --> 00:35:04,227
Know what I mean, Kihyun?

447
00:35:09,482 --> 00:35:10,691
Oh, by the way,

448
00:35:10,692 --> 00:35:12,569
there's something I need you to do.

449
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:17,740
Keep close tabs on what happens
at the JIH and report back to me.

450
00:35:17,741 --> 00:35:19,826
So I'm supposed to act as your mole now?

451
00:35:20,577 --> 00:35:22,287
The fact is we're at war.

452
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:25,122
And it won't end until one side falls.

453
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:30,629
Our whole family will go down
if I'm the one who falls.

454
00:35:45,143 --> 00:35:47,228
It's amazing how you always do this.

455
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:52,359
You can't hold our family captive forever.

456
00:35:57,489 --> 00:35:58,657
Are you saying

457
00:36:00,033 --> 00:36:01,785
you want to go against me?

458
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:53,837
I've got the money ready.

459
00:36:54,546 --> 00:36:56,130
How long 'til it gets here?

460
00:36:56,131 --> 00:36:58,298
Around two days. I'm gonna bring it.

461
00:36:58,299 --> 00:36:59,967
You mean you personally?

462
00:36:59,968 --> 00:37:02,469
Of course. It's a hefty sum.

463
00:37:02,470 --> 00:37:04,596
Besides, we have some things to discuss.

464
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,224
Really? Like what?

465
00:37:09,102 --> 00:37:12,312
Well, martial law's putting quite a dent
in our sales.

466
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:13,648
So we better strategize.

467
00:37:15,734 --> 00:37:17,861
All right, then. I'll be waiting for you.

468
00:37:42,051 --> 00:37:43,470
Morning, sir!

469
00:37:50,602 --> 00:37:51,811
What, Captain Min?

470
00:37:52,520 --> 00:37:55,773
Oh. You're needed
at Joint Investigation Headquarters.

471
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:58,484
- The Colonel requested your presence.
- Really?

472
00:37:58,485 --> 00:37:59,486
Yes, sir.

473
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:12,373
Is there something else?

474
00:38:13,041 --> 00:38:14,125
Uh…

475
00:38:14,876 --> 00:38:18,213
Rumor is they've been planning
to increase their personnel.

476
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:19,964
And?

477
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:22,675
Would you recommend me?

478
00:38:29,057 --> 00:38:31,975
I heard about you
from the Busan Prosecutors' Office.

479
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:33,561
You're kinda famous over there.

480
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:36,480
Nah, that's really not true.

481
00:38:36,481 --> 00:38:40,359
I keep the wheels turning, that's all.
Just try to keep the place on track.

482
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:41,985
- Smooth things over.
- Mm-hmm.

483
00:38:41,986 --> 00:38:43,321
Well, that's not what I heard.

484
00:38:43,947 --> 00:38:46,074
There are some colorful stories.

485
00:38:46,991 --> 00:38:47,992
Oh, really?

486
00:38:48,535 --> 00:38:50,118
They say I'm outta my goddamn mind?

487
00:38:51,663 --> 00:38:52,996
Hear that?

488
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:55,666
That funny to you?

489
00:38:55,667 --> 00:38:58,502
- Uh, no. It's, uh, not funny at all.
-  Hey, hand me that stapler.

490
00:38:58,503 --> 00:38:59,587
No, no, sorry, uh…

491
00:39:00,421 --> 00:39:02,173
No one said you're crazy really.

492
00:39:02,924 --> 00:39:04,967
More like prone to impulsivity, reckless.

493
00:39:04,968 --> 00:39:06,594
Look, I have self-control.

494
00:39:07,846 --> 00:39:09,721
I just don't like to bother with it.

495
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:13,350
Am I supposed to be a hall monitor
or am I supposed to bust criminals?

496
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:15,435
- Who cares how I do it?
- Just like I heard.

497
00:39:15,436 --> 00:39:16,938
You've got a big pair of balls on you.

498
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:38,334
Ah. There he is.

499
00:39:40,086 --> 00:39:41,254
Oh, Colonel Baek!

500
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:46,633
Say hello.

501
00:39:46,634 --> 00:39:49,052
She works
in the Busan District Prosecutors' Office.

502
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:50,054
Oh Yejin. It's a pleasure.

503
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:52,015
Baek Kihyun, ma'am.

504
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:54,684
Nice to meet you. How's your sister?

505
00:39:56,769 --> 00:39:59,187
You know her? You two met?

506
00:39:59,188 --> 00:40:01,189
Yeah, in Busan, I knew her…

507
00:40:01,190 --> 00:40:04,152
…not super well,
just a little bit.

508
00:40:04,903 --> 00:40:05,986
I see.

509
00:40:05,987 --> 00:40:07,614
Yeah, all right.

510
00:40:08,656 --> 00:40:11,159
Okay, Ms. Oh, everything's ready.
We should head out now.

511
00:40:11,784 --> 00:40:13,827
Uh-huh. Let's move then.

512
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:15,204
See you around, Mr. Baek.

513
00:40:16,289 --> 00:40:17,372
All right, move it!

514
00:40:17,373 --> 00:40:18,499
- Okay.
- Yes, ma'am.

515
00:40:20,168 --> 00:40:22,252
-  Goodbye.
-  Hey, grab the radios.

516
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:24,422
This way. There's someone you should meet.

517
00:40:31,346 --> 00:40:32,513
Close the door.

518
00:40:33,681 --> 00:40:34,682
Have a seat.

519
00:40:37,393 --> 00:40:39,102
So who am I meeting?

520
00:40:39,103 --> 00:40:40,772
Well actually, you know him already.

521
00:40:43,650 --> 00:40:47,235
He'll be here soon.
So let's have a smoke while we're waiting.

522
00:40:47,236 --> 00:40:48,279
Sure.

523
00:41:08,174 --> 00:41:09,299
Let's see.

524
00:41:09,300 --> 00:41:11,260
All right. We've got a few minutes.

525
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:31,656
- Sir.
- Thanks.

526
00:41:32,532 --> 00:41:33,574
Here.

527
00:41:40,832 --> 00:41:43,291
The raw materials are coming today,
you're sure?

528
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:44,502
Yes, I'm sure.

529
00:41:53,803 --> 00:41:55,555
I heard you're going to Busan.

530
00:41:56,806 --> 00:41:58,182
Why make the trip, sir?

531
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:00,476
I've got some business.

532
00:42:01,019 --> 00:42:02,395
What kind?

533
00:42:05,231 --> 00:42:07,275
Do I have to tell you everything?

534
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:10,361
Just making conversation.

535
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:23,665
Director, the car is ready for you.

536
00:42:23,666 --> 00:42:25,126
Okay.

537
00:42:25,710 --> 00:42:26,711
You're going along?

538
00:42:29,589 --> 00:42:30,590
Yes.

539
00:42:34,427 --> 00:42:36,679
You never even called
once you moved to Seoul.

540
00:42:37,263 --> 00:42:39,598
I apologize.
I've been getting settled in Seoul.

541
00:42:39,599 --> 00:42:41,142
- I'm busy.
- You goddamn little shit.

542
00:42:42,310 --> 00:42:44,853
- Sir?
- What's with your tone?

543
00:42:44,854 --> 00:42:46,688
What about my tone?

544
00:42:46,689 --> 00:42:48,024
- Hey!
- You…

545
00:42:52,653 --> 00:42:53,905
The hell are you doing?

546
00:42:59,869 --> 00:43:01,829
Do what I told you. I expect some results.

547
00:43:02,789 --> 00:43:03,790
Yes, Mr. Baek, sir.

548
00:43:04,707 --> 00:43:06,459
- Let's go.
- I'll see you when you're back.

549
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:21,015
Boys,

550
00:43:22,809 --> 00:43:24,185
be ambitious!

551
00:43:55,049 --> 00:43:56,425
It's Haksu. Hello.

552
00:43:58,427 --> 00:44:01,139
1:08 A.M., BUSAN

553
00:44:44,265 --> 00:44:45,473
Okay. They're on the move.

554
00:44:45,474 --> 00:44:50,146
1:15 A.M., SEOUL

555
00:44:51,063 --> 00:44:53,608
Ms. Oh. They just arrived.

556
00:45:22,220 --> 00:45:26,515
BAEKHO TRADING INC.

557
00:45:35,608 --> 00:45:39,904
1:38 A.M., BUSAN

558
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:46,535
What's your plan now?

559
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:50,831
What's all this money going to be for?

560
00:45:52,041 --> 00:45:53,209
Patriotism.

561
00:46:01,092 --> 00:46:03,844
How? With a showdown?
You gonna start some kind of gunfight?

562
00:46:05,638 --> 00:46:07,265
Well, I've come this far.

563
00:46:08,099 --> 00:46:09,308
Can't stop now.

564
00:46:12,979 --> 00:46:14,438
Are you sure you can pull it off?

565
00:46:15,398 --> 00:46:17,149
Honestly, I'm not sure that matters.

566
00:46:19,944 --> 00:46:21,737
All that matters in a gunfight is

567
00:46:23,364 --> 00:46:25,074
who's faster on the draw.

568
00:46:32,373 --> 00:46:33,499
Open fire!

569
00:46:35,209 --> 00:46:36,335
Get down!

570
00:47:29,263 --> 00:47:30,264
Long time no see.
